<spell-notebook "avatar usage">
	<header level="1">
		Avatar
		<header>An avatar is a small picture of a person, beside a comment, an item or a card.</header>
	</header>
	<avatar-tab-bar showing="usage"/>

	<section label="Using it">
		<markdown>
			`<ui-avatar>` is a small picture of a person: a comment's, an item's or a card's.

			- `src` renders the `<img>`; or slot your own `<img>`.
			- `alt` defaults to `""` (decorative): the person's name is right beside it. Give it text when it isn't.
			- Its look comes from its owner: 2.5em beside a comment, 2em and round inline in a card, round in an item.
		</markdown>
	</section>

	<section label="Owners">
		<markdown>
			`<ui-avatar>` finds its nearest owner and sets `:state(in-<owner>)` on itself; `UIParts.css` styles it by that
			state. Its owners, and what each makes of it:

			- [Comment](/components/ui/ui-comment.html) (`:state(in-comment)`): beside the content, on the left
			- [Card](/components/ui/ui-card.html) (`:state(in-card)`): small and round, inline before a name
			- [Item](/components/ui/ui-items.html) (`:state(in-item)`): round, inline before a name

			Anywhere else it is an unstyled block. More on how parts find their owners: [Content parts](/components/ui/ui-header.html#usage-owners).
		</markdown>
	</section>

	<section label="Accessibility">
		<markdown>
			- `alt` defaults to `""`, so the image is decorative: the name next to it already says who it is. Set `alt` (or
			  slot an `<img alt>`) when the avatar stands alone.
			- No role of its own, no tab stop.
		</markdown>
	</section>
</spell-notebook>
